-- הסכם קיבוצי — רפורמה לתנאי עבודתם של המדריכים (9.11.2016), "הסכם
-- המדריכים": the reform of the pay of teaching employees in guidance roles
-- ("מדריכים"), from 1.9.2016, for the part of the position they guide in.
-- Who it covers; the work week unchanged, the days of guidance the Ministry
-- sets, the parallel teaching role and the attendance clock; the
-- definitions — the three pay terms a guide's base salary may follow (Ofek
-- Hadash, Oz LaTmura, the colleges), an interruption, the determining month,
-- the full guide and the regular guide; the regular guide's pay: the base
-- salary by where he taught in the determining month, the guidance allowance
-- by his days of guidance, the profession allowance for those on Oz LaTmura
-- or college terms, and the trailing supplements offset against them; when
-- it is paid; the determining salary of a budgetary pension; and the earlier
-- agreements, exhaustion of claims, industrial peace and the follow-up
-- committee.
--
-- The annex the agreement names (annex א', the list of full guides) is not
-- in the document as the corpus holds it: an input. The Director-General's
-- circular תשס"ד/2(ב), the collective agreements of the Oz LaTmura reform and
-- of the colleges (7.5.2015), the pension letters of 11.5.2016 and
-- 21.12.2015 are not in the corpus: what a rule needs of them is a named
-- input.
--
-- Imported: the base agreement's §2 (language) and §155 (the further
-- populations, which §20 exhausts for the guides); the completion agreement
-- of 29.2.2012 (its §90, which §20 exhausts for the guides, and the
-- populations its §85 lists); and the agreement of 30.9.2016 (its §11(ב)(1),
-- which §20 exhausts, and the agreement §13(ב) takes away from a guide on Oz
-- LaTmura terms). The 2022 wage agreement's §2 names this agreement as "the
-- guides' agreement of 9.11.2016" (§12(ב)–(ג) there).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT parties
IMPORT `base-agreement-2`
IMPORT `base-agreement-155`
IMPORT `2012-02-29_ofek-hadash_amendment_hascam-hashlama`
IMPORT `2016-09-30_ofek-hadash_september-2016-agreement`

-- A salary month: the salary paid FOR month m of year y (convention
-- dates.salary-month).
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `guides' agreement salary month` y m IS
    y TIMES 12 PLUS m

-- A school year named by the calendar year it opens in: תשע"ו is 2015,
-- תשע"ז 2016, תשע"ח 2017.

-- What the parties and the guides must, may or may not do under this
-- agreement.
DECLARE `guides' agreement action` IS ONE OF
    `set the guide's days of guidance in a week`
    `sign in and out on the electronic attendance clock`
    `report the hours of presence as the Ministry sets`
    `discuss the pay of a guide who is neither regular nor full`
    `act to recognise the guidance allowance as a fixed supplement for the Pensions Law`
    `make pension-fund contributions on the guidance allowance`
    `make study-fund contributions on the guidance allowance`
    `pay the payments of chapter ה`
    `act in the spirit of §19 on a matter the agreement did not discuss`
    `negotiate a matter §20(א) exhausts`
    `negotiate further economic demands on the reform for the guides`
    `strike, lock out or disrupt work over a matter the guides' agreement settles`

§ `הסכם המדריכים — 9.11.2016`

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The document's title; no rule.

-- The day of signing, written in by hand.
@ref akn:preamble/p2
`the guides' agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 9 11 2016

-- akn:preamble/p3 The Registrar's stamp: registered on 15.01.2017 as no. 283/2016; no rule of the agreement.
-- akn:preamble/p4 A second registration stamp, left blank; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p5 The note that pages 1–8 are signed in the margin; no rule.

-- The parties: the State, by the Treasury's acting wages commissioner and
-- the Ministry of Education's director-general, and the teachers' union, by
-- its secretary-general.
@ref akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p9 akn:preamble/p10
`the guides' agreement's parties` MEANS LIST `the State`, `the teachers' union`

-- akn:preamble/p8 "On the one side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p11 "On the other side"; no rule.

-- The recitals: the agreements of 10.9.07 and 25.12.08 on the reform; the
-- base agreement's promise to negotiate a reform for teaching employees in
-- guidance roles (its §155(ב), imported); the State's decision on a reform
-- of the guides' work ("הרפורמה בהדרכה"); guides are placed each year, for
-- that year, with no tenure in the role; the pay structure agreed; the rise
-- in pay; the determining salary of a budgetary pension computed over two
-- periods. They state the history; the rules are below.
@ref akn:preamble/p12 akn:preamble/p13
`the base agreement promised a reform for the guides` MEANS
    `may be negotiated` `the reform for further populations`

#ASSERT `the base agreement promised a reform for the guides`

@ref akn:preamble/p14 akn:preamble/p15
`a guide has tenure in the guidance role` MEANS FALSE

@ref akn:preamble/p16 akn:preamble/p17 akn:preamble/p18
`the guides' determining salary is computed over two periods` MEANS TRUE

-- akn:preamble/p19 A recital: the parties anchor what they agreed in a collective agreement; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p20 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.

§§ `א. כללי (1–4)`

-- akn:part_1 The heading of chapter א (general); its clauses follow.

-- §1: the preamble and the annex are an inseparable part of the agreement.
@ref akn:art_1
GIVEN p IS A `part of the agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an inseparable part of the guides' agreement` p IF
    TRUE

-- §2: the masculine includes the feminine, the singular the plural, and
-- the reverse, unless said otherwise expressly: the base agreement's §2.
@ref akn:art_2
GIVEN `written in` IS A `form of a word`, `read in` IS A `form of a word`, `expressly limited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a word of the guides' agreement reads in another form` `written in` `read in` `expressly limited` IF
    `a word written in one form reads in another` `written in` `read in` `expressly limited`

-- §3: the headings are for convenience and do not bear on the reading.
@ref akn:art_3
GIVEN `the reading without the headings` IS A STRING, `the reading the headings suggest` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the reading the guides' agreement takes` `the reading without the headings` `the reading the headings suggest` IS
    `the reading without the headings`

-- §4: mentioning a Director-General's circular or a letter does not change
-- its normative standing.
@ref akn:art_4
GIVEN `its standing` IS A NUMBER, `mentioned in this agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the standing of an instrument the guides' agreement mentions` `its standing` `mentioned in this agreement` IS
    `its standing`

§§ `ב. תחולה ותחילה (5–6)`

-- akn:part_2 The heading of chapter ב; its clauses follow.

@desc An employee, as far as §5 of the guides' agreement asks.
DECLARE `employee under the guides' agreement` HAS
    `in the State's service`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `graded on the teaching employees' scale`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by the Ministry in a guidance role under circular תשס"ד/2(ב)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the Director-General's circular, as amended from time to time; not in the corpus
    `still serving in the role`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `his guidance share`                              IS A NUMBER
    `his share in other roles`                        IS A NUMBER @desc teaching employment in the State's service in other roles

-- §5: every employee in the State's service, graded on the teaching
-- employees' scale and employed by the Ministry in guidance roles by
-- circular תשס"ד/2(ב), while he serves in it ("מדריכים"); ¶2: one employed
-- in other roles too is covered for the part of the position he guides in.
@ref akn:art_5 akn:art_5/p2
GIVEN e IS AN `employee under the guides' agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a guide under the guides' agreement` e IF
        e's `in the State's service`
    AND e's `graded on the teaching employees' scale`
    AND e's `employed by the Ministry in a guidance role under circular תשס"ד/2(ב)`
    AND e's `still serving in the role`

GIVEN e IS AN `employee under the guides' agreement`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of the position the guides' agreement covers` e IS
    IF `a guide under the guides' agreement` e
    THEN e's `his guidance share`
    ELSE 0

-- §6: it starts on 1.9.2016 ("המועד הקובע").
@ref akn:art_6
`the guides' agreement's determining date` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016

#ASSERT `the guides' agreement's determining date` EQUALS `the September 2016 determining date`

§§ `ג. מבנה שבוע העבודה וסדרי עבודה (7–9)`

-- akn:part_3 The heading of chapter ג; its clauses follow.

-- §7: the reform does not change the guides' work week or hours, as they
-- were before it, by the Director-General's circulars from time to time.
@ref akn:art_7
`the guides' reform changes the work week or the hours` MEANS FALSE

-- §8: nor does it take from the Ministry's power to set, at its
-- discretion, a guide's employment at half a day of guidance a week, or from
-- one to four days.
@ref akn:art_8
GIVEN `days of guidance a week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `days the Ministry may set for a guide` `days of guidance a week` IF
       `days of guidance a week` EQUALS 0.5
    OR (`days of guidance a week` AT LEAST 1 AND `days of guidance a week` AT MOST 4)

@ref akn:art_8
`setting the days of guidance` MEANS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MAY   `set the guide's days of guidance in a week`

#ASSERT `days the Ministry may set for a guide` 0.5
#ASSERT NOT `days the Ministry may set for a guide` 5

-- §9: a condition of employment as a guide is employment by the
-- Director-General's circulars on guides — among them a parallel teaching
-- role that is not guidance, at the least position they set (an input).
@ref akn:art_9
ASSUME `the least teaching position the circulars ask of a guide` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `employed by the circulars on guides` IS A BOOLEAN, `share of the position in other roles` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be employed as a guide` `employed by the circulars on guides` `share of the position in other roles` IF
        `employed by the circulars on guides`
    AND `share of the position in other roles` AT LEAST `the least teaching position the circulars ask of a guide`

§§ `ד. שעון נוכחות (10)`

-- akn:part_4 The heading of chapter ד; its clause follows.

-- §10: from the school year תשע"ז, a guide under the reform signs in and
-- out on the electronic attendance clock at every entry to and exit from
-- the institution or office he guides in; where there is none, he reports
-- his hours as the Ministry sets.
@ref akn:art_10
`the attendance clock from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016

GIVEN `the place has an electronic clock` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `guides' agreement action`
DECIDE `a guide's attendance` `the place has an electronic clock` IS
    IF `the place has an electronic clock`
    THEN PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MUST  `sign in and out on the electronic attendance clock`
    ELSE PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MUST  `report the hours of presence as the Ministry sets`

§§ `ה. שכר המדריכים בתנאי הרפורמה (11–21)`

-- akn:part_5 The heading of chapter ה; its clauses follow.
-- akn:art_11 The definitions' lead-in ("בהסכם זה:"); the definitions follow.

-- §11, the three terms: "תנאי רפורמת אופק חדש" — the salary a teaching
-- employee would be paid that year as a teacher in an institution in the
-- State's service under Ofek Hadash, by his placement on its tables and his
-- position; "תנאי רפורמת עוז לתמורה" — as a teacher in a three- or four-year
-- upper division supervised by the Ministry, on Oz LaTmura terms;
-- "תנאי ההעסקה במכללות" — as a teacher in a college that trains teaching
-- employees, by its agreements (7.5.2015 among them). None includes role
-- allowances or pay supplements that turn on performance. Each is an input.
DECLARE `terms a guide's base salary follows` IS ONE OF
    `Ofek Hadash terms for the guide`
    `Oz LaTmura terms for the guide`
    `the colleges' terms for the guide`
    `the guides' terms before the agreement`

@ref akn:art_11/p1 akn:art_11/p2 akn:art_11/p3
ASSUME `the salary the terms pay for the position` IS A FUNCTION FROM `terms a guide's base salary follows` AND NUMBER TO NUMBER

@ref akn:art_11/p1 akn:art_11/p2 akn:art_11/p3
`the terms include role allowances or performance supplements` MEANS FALSE

-- "הפסקה בהעסקה בתפקיד הדרכה": a school year for which the employee was not
-- appointed in writing to a guidance role, by the Ministry's directions. ¶5:
-- the rules of seniority in guidance do not change.
@ref akn:art_11/p4 akn:art_11/p5
GIVEN `appointed in writing to a guidance role that year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a year of interruption in guidance` `appointed in writing to a guidance role that year` IF
    NOT `appointed in writing to a guidance role that year`

`the guides' agreement changes the rules of seniority in guidance` MEANS FALSE

-- "החודש הקובע": for one appointed in תשע"ז (whether or not he guided
-- before), May of תשע"ו; for one first appointed from תשע"ח on, May of the
-- school year before; for one appointed again from תשע"ח on after an
-- interruption, May of the school year before the new appointment — each
-- so long as no interruption follows. A school year opening in year y has
-- its May in y + 1, so the May of the year before is in y.
@ref akn:art_11/p6 akn:art_11/p7 akn:art_11/p8
GIVEN `the school year of the appointment opens in` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the guide's determining month` `the school year of the appointment opens in` IS
    `guides' agreement salary month` `the school year of the appointment opens in` 5

#ASSERT `the guide's determining month` 2016 EQUALS `guides' agreement salary month` 2016 5
#ASSERT `the guide's determining month` 2017 EQUALS `guides' agreement salary month` 2017 5

-- "מדריך מלא": a guide employed, exceptionally, six days of guidance a week
-- on the eve of the signing, listed in annex א' (not in the corpus: an
-- input).
@ref akn:art_11/p9
GIVEN `days of guidance a week on the eve of the signing` IS A NUMBER, `listed in annex א'` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a full guide` `days of guidance a week on the eve of the signing` `listed in annex א'` IF
    `days of guidance a week on the eve of the signing` EQUALS 6 AND `listed in annex א'`

@desc Where a guide taught (not as a guide) in the determining month, as far as §§11 and 13 ask.
DECLARE `guide's teaching in the determining month` HAS
    `in an institution in the State's service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a school or institution in the State's service as the base agreement means one, save upper divisions
    `in an upper division`                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc a three- or four-year upper division the Ministry supervises, or one in a State school
    `in a college that trains teaching employees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as a Shelach teacher`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `elsewhere`                                IS A BOOLEAN

-- "מדריך מוסדר": a guide who in the determining month taught, in all or
-- part of his teaching (not guidance) position, in one or more of (1) an
-- institution in the State's service, (2) an upper division, (3) a college.
@ref akn:art_11/p10 akn:art_11__para_1 akn:art_11__para_2 akn:art_11__para_3
GIVEN w IS A `guide's teaching in the determining month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a regular guide` w IF
       w's `in an institution in the State's service`
    OR w's `in an upper division`
    OR w's `in a college that trains teaching employees`

-- §12: (א) a regular guide's pay is made of §§13–17; (ב) a full guide keeps
-- the guides' pay before the agreement, and §§13–18 do not apply to him;
-- (ג) the pay of a guide who is neither is discussed after the signing, and
-- until agreed he keeps the pay before it — without taking from the
-- industrial peace of §20 (¶2).
DECLARE `kind of guide` IS ONE OF
    `a regular guide, by §11`
    `a full guide, by §11`
    `a guide who is neither regular nor full`

@ref akn:art_12 akn:art_12__para_a akn:art_12__para_b akn:art_12__para_c akn:art_12__para_c/p2
GIVEN k IS A `kind of guide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid by §§13–17 of the guides' agreement` k IF
    k EQUALS `a regular guide, by §11`

@ref akn:art_12__para_c
`discussing the pay of the other guides` MEANS
    (PARTY `the State`
     MAY   `discuss the pay of a guide who is neither regular nor full`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     MAY   `discuss the pay of a guide who is neither regular nor full`)

-- §13(א): from the determining date, a regular guide's base salary for his
-- guidance part, from the school year after the determining month, follows
-- (1) Ofek Hadash terms if he taught only in an institution in the State's
-- service; (2) Oz LaTmura terms if only in an upper division; (3) the
-- colleges' terms if only in a college; (4) Ofek Hadash terms if in an
-- institution in the State's service and in an upper division or a college
-- or both; (5) Oz LaTmura terms if in an upper division and a college; (6)
-- notwithstanding (1)–(5), Ofek Hadash terms if he taught as a Shelach
-- teacher; (7) teaching elsewhere besides changes nothing (¶2).
@ref akn:art_13 akn:art_13__para_a akn:art_13__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_13__para_a__subpara_2 akn:art_13__para_a__subpara_3 akn:art_13__para_a__subpara_4 akn:art_13__para_a__subpara_5 akn:art_13__para_a__subpara_6 akn:art_13__para_a__subpara_7 akn:art_13__para_a__subpara_7/p2
GIVEN w IS A `guide's teaching in the determining month`
GIVETH A `terms a guide's base salary follows`
DECIDE `the terms of a regular guide's base salary` w IS
    BRANCH
        IF w's `as a Shelach teacher` THEN `Ofek Hadash terms for the guide`
        IF w's `in an institution in the State's service` THEN `Ofek Hadash terms for the guide`
        IF w's `in an upper division` THEN `Oz LaTmura terms for the guide`
        IF w's `in a college that trains teaching employees` THEN `the colleges' terms for the guide`
        OTHERWISE `the guides' terms before the agreement`

GIVEN s IS A BOOLEAN, u IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, h IS A BOOLEAN, o IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `guide's teaching in the determining month`
DECIDE `a guide who taught in` s u c h o IS
    `guide's teaching in the determining month` WITH
        `in an institution in the State's service` IS s
        `in an upper division`                     IS u
        `in a college that trains teaching employees` IS c
        `as a Shelach teacher`                     IS h
        `elsewhere`                                IS o

-- Every combination of the three places has one terms, as (1)–(5) list
-- them, and teaching elsewhere besides changes none of them.
#ASSERT `the terms of a regular guide's base salary` (`a guide who taught in` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `Ofek Hadash terms for the guide`
#ASSERT `the terms of a regular guide's base salary` (`a guide who taught in` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `Oz LaTmura terms for the guide`
#ASSERT `the terms of a regular guide's base salary` (`a guide who taught in` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the colleges' terms for the guide`
#ASSERT `the terms of a regular guide's base salary` (`a guide who taught in` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `Ofek Hadash terms for the guide`
#ASSERT `the terms of a regular guide's base salary` (`a guide who taught in` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `Oz LaTmura terms for the guide`
#ASSERT `the terms of a regular guide's base salary` (`a guide who taught in` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `Ofek Hadash terms for the guide`
#ASSERT NOT `a regular guide` (`a guide who taught in` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

-- The examples (¶2–¶3): appointed in תשע"ח, in May of תשע"ז he taught in an
-- institution in the State's service, an upper division and elsewhere: Ofek
-- Hadash terms; in a college and elsewhere: the colleges' terms.
@ref akn:art_13__para_a/p2 akn:art_13__para_a/p3
`the example's first guide` MEANS `a guide who taught in` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`the example's second guide` MEANS `a guide who taught in` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT `the terms of a regular guide's base salary` `the example's first guide` EQUALS `Ofek Hadash terms for the guide`
#ASSERT `the terms of a regular guide's base salary` `the example's second guide` EQUALS `the colleges' terms for the guide`

-- The school year from which the terms apply: the one that opens after the
-- determining month (§13(א)).
GIVEN `the determining month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the school year the guide's terms apply from opens in` `the determining month` IS
    FLOOR ((`the determining month` MINUS 9) DIVIDED BY 12) PLUS 1

#ASSERT `the school year the guide's terms apply from opens in` (`guides' agreement salary month` 2016 5) EQUALS 2016

-- The base salary for the guidance part: the terms' salary for that part.
GIVEN k IS A `kind of guide`
      w IS A `guide's teaching in the determining month`
      `share of the position in guidance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a guide's base salary for the guidance part` k w `share of the position in guidance` IS
    IF `paid by §§13–17 of the guides' agreement` k
    THEN `the salary the terms pay for the position` (`the terms of a regular guide's base salary` w) `share of the position in guidance`
    ELSE `the salary the terms pay for the position` `the guides' terms before the agreement` `share of the position in guidance`

-- §13(ב)–(ג): a guide whose base salary follows (א)(2) or (5) — Oz LaTmura
-- terms — is not entitled, for the guidance part, to the pay and terms of
-- the collective agreements of teaching employees in institutions in the
-- State's service, the agreement of 30.9.2016 to 30.6.2018 among them
-- (imported: its shekel supplement); save their pension terms, which apply
-- to him subject to §18. (ד): from the determining date §13 replaces the
-- rules before it on the guidance part's pay.
@ref akn:art_13__para_b akn:art_13__para_c akn:art_13__para_d
DECLARE `kind of term of the State institutions' agreements` IS ONE OF
    `a pay term of those agreements`
    `a pension term of those agreements`

GIVEN t IS A `terms a guide's base salary follows`, k IS A `kind of term of the State institutions' agreements`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the State institutions' agreements reach the guidance part` t k IF
    (NOT t EQUALS `Oz LaTmura terms for the guide`) OR k EQUALS `a pension term of those agreements`

GIVEN t IS A `terms a guide's base salary follows`
      ps IS A LIST OF `shekel supplement period`
      decembers IS A LIST OF `December index`
      `share of the position in guidance` IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the September 2016 shekel supplement for the guidance part` t ps decembers `share of the position in guidance` d IS
    IF `the State institutions' agreements reach the guidance part` t `a pay term of those agreements`
    THEN `the shekel supplement for a teaching employee` ps decembers `share of the position in guidance` d
    ELSE 0

#ASSERT `the September 2016 shekel supplement for the guidance part` `Oz LaTmura terms for the guide` `the September 2016 shekel supplement periods` `hypothetical December indices` 0.5 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2016) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the State institutions' agreements reach the guidance part` `Oz LaTmura terms for the guide` `a pension term of those agreements`

@ref akn:art_13__para_d
`the guides' pay rules before the agreement govern a regular guide's guidance part` MEANS FALSE

-- §14(א): on top of the base salary, a regular guide is entitled to the
-- guidance allowance: the components that are the base of percentage
-- allowances under his terms, at their value for a full position, times
-- the rate by his days of guidance: half a day (8.33% of a position) 3%; one
-- day (16.67%) 6%; two (33.33%) 15%; three (50%) 17.5%; four (66.67%) 20%.
@ref akn:art_14 akn:art_14__para_a akn:art_14__para_a/p2 akn:art_14__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_14__para_a__subpara_2 akn:art_14__para_a__subpara_3 akn:art_14__para_a__subpara_4 akn:art_14__para_a__subpara_5
GIVEN `days of guidance a week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the guidance allowance rate` `days of guidance a week` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `days of guidance a week` EQUALS 0.5 THEN JUST (3%)
        IF `days of guidance a week` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST (6%)
        IF `days of guidance a week` EQUALS 2 THEN JUST (15%)
        IF `days of guidance a week` EQUALS 3 THEN JUST (17.5%)
        IF `days of guidance a week` EQUALS 4 THEN JUST (20%)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `days of guidance a week` IS A NUMBER, `the full-position base of percentage allowances` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the guidance allowance` `days of guidance a week` `the full-position base of percentage allowances` IS
    CONSIDER `the guidance allowance rate` `days of guidance a week`
    WHEN JUST r THEN r TIMES `the full-position base of percentage allowances`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

-- A day of guidance is a sixth of a position, as the shares the clause
-- prints show, to the hundredth of a percent.
#ASSERT `to the nearest` (2 DIVIDED BY 6) 0.0001 EQUALS 33.33%
#ASSERT `to the nearest` (0.5 DIVIDED BY 6) 0.0001 EQUALS 8.33%
#ASSERT `to the nearest` (4 DIVIDED BY 6) 0.0001 EQUALS 66.67%
#ASSERT `the guidance allowance` 2 12000 EQUALS 1800

-- (ב): from the determining date §14 replaces the earlier rules on the
-- guidance allowance; (ג): it is the base of no percentage allowance; (ד):
-- the State undertakes to act to recognise it as a fixed supplement for the
-- Pensions Law; (ה): pension contributions for those insured in an accrual
-- pension; (ו): study-fund contributions.
@ref akn:art_14__para_b akn:art_14__para_c
`the guidance allowance is a base of percentage allowances` MEANS FALSE

@ref akn:art_14__para_d
`recognising the guidance allowance for pension` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `act to recognise the guidance allowance as a fixed supplement for the Pensions Law`

@ref akn:art_14__para_e akn:art_14__para_f
GIVEN `insured in an accrual pension on the determining salary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `guides' agreement action`
DECIDE `contributions on the guidance allowance` `insured in an accrual pension on the determining salary` IS
    IF `insured in an accrual pension on the determining salary`
    THEN (PARTY `the State` MUST `make pension-fund contributions on the guidance allowance`)
         RAND
         (PARTY `the State` MUST `make study-fund contributions on the guidance allowance`)
    ELSE PARTY `the State` MUST `make study-fund contributions on the guidance allowance`

-- §15(א): on top of the base salary and the guidance allowance, a regular
-- guide paid on Oz LaTmura or the colleges' terms is entitled, for the
-- guidance part, to the profession and training allowance by those terms'
-- rules and in proportion to that part — even if he is not entitled to it
-- for his other part. (ב): his entitlement for the other part is by those
-- terms' own rules; §15 creates none. The allowance by those rules is an
-- input.
@ref akn:art_15 akn:art_15__para_a akn:art_15__para_b
ASSUME `the profession allowance by the terms' rules for a full position` IS A FUNCTION FROM `terms a guide's base salary follows` TO NUMBER

GIVEN t IS A `terms a guide's base salary follows`, `share of the position in guidance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the profession allowance for the guidance part` t `share of the position in guidance` IF
        (t EQUALS `Oz LaTmura terms for the guide` OR t EQUALS `the colleges' terms for the guide`)
    AND `share of the position in guidance` GREATER THAN 0

GIVEN t IS A `terms a guide's base salary follows`, `share of the position in guidance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the profession allowance for the guidance part` t `share of the position in guidance` IS
    IF `entitled to the profession allowance for the guidance part` t `share of the position in guidance`
    THEN (`the profession allowance by the terms' rules for a full position` t) `pro rata to a position of` `share of the position in guidance`
    ELSE 0

`§15 creates a profession allowance for the other part` MEANS FALSE

-- §16(א): notwithstanding any other collective agreement, a regular guide
-- entitled for his other part to one of the supplements of (ד) — a trailing
-- management allowance, a trailing counselling allowance, a salary-
-- protection supplement of §38ב, §38ג or §50א of the base agreement ("תוספת
-- שמירת שכר") — has it for the guidance part only if (1) he has no
-- profession allowance for that part and the supplement, in proportion to
-- that part, is higher than his guidance allowance, or (2) he has the
-- profession allowance and the supplement is higher than it and the
-- guidance allowance together. (ב): with (1), no guidance allowance; with
-- (2), neither the guidance allowance nor the profession allowance.
-- F-ofek-hadash-madrichim-2016-a: §16 sends the profession allowance to
-- "§16 above" (it is §15's), the guidance allowance to "§15 above" (it is
-- §14's), its list to "sub-clause (ה) below" (it is (ד)), and (ב) to
-- "§§15 and 16 above" (they are §§14 and 15). The reading adopted
-- (convention reading.misprint): each is read as the clause that says what
-- the reference names.
DECLARE `trailing supplement of §16(ד)` IS ONE OF
    `a trailing management allowance`
    `a trailing counselling allowance`
    `a salary-protection supplement of §38ב, §38ג or §50א of the base agreement`

@desc A regular guide's allowances for the guidance part, as §16 sets them against each other.
DECLARE `guide's allowances for the guidance part` HAS
    `the trailing supplement in proportion to the guidance part` IS A NUMBER @desc 0 where he has none of (ד)'s supplements
    `the guidance allowance computed`                IS A NUMBER
    `the profession allowance computed`              IS A NUMBER
    `entitled to the profession allowance`           IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `what §16 pays for the guidance part` IS ONE OF
    `the guidance allowance, and the profession allowance if entitled`
    `the trailing supplement instead of the guidance allowance`
    `the trailing supplement instead of both allowances`

@ref akn:art_16 akn:art_16__para_a akn:art_16__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_16__para_a__subpara_2 akn:art_16__para_b akn:art_16__para_d akn:art_16__para_d__subpara_1 akn:art_16__para_d__subpara_2 akn:art_16__para_d__subpara_3
GIVEN a IS A `guide's allowances for the guidance part`
GIVETH A `what §16 pays for the guidance part`
DECIDE `§16 of the guides' agreement pays` a IS
    IF a's `entitled to the profession allowance`
    THEN (IF a's `the trailing supplement in proportion to the guidance part` GREATER THAN a's `the guidance allowance computed` PLUS a's `the profession allowance computed`
          THEN `the trailing supplement instead of both allowances`
          ELSE `the guidance allowance, and the profession allowance if entitled`)
    ELSE (IF a's `the trailing supplement in proportion to the guidance part` GREATER THAN a's `the guidance allowance computed`
          THEN `the trailing supplement instead of the guidance allowance`
          ELSE `the guidance allowance, and the profession allowance if entitled`)

GIVEN a IS A `guide's allowances for the guidance part`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the guidance part's allowances under §16` a IS
    CONSIDER `§16 of the guides' agreement pays` a
    WHEN `the trailing supplement instead of the guidance allowance` THEN a's `the trailing supplement in proportion to the guidance part` PLUS a's `the profession allowance computed`
    WHEN `the trailing supplement instead of both allowances` THEN a's `the trailing supplement in proportion to the guidance part`
    WHEN `the guidance allowance, and the profession allowance if entitled` THEN
        a's `the guidance allowance computed` PLUS (IF a's `entitled to the profession allowance` THEN a's `the profession allowance computed` ELSE 0)

#ASSERT `the guidance part's allowances under §16` (`guide's allowances for the guidance part` 2000 1800 0 FALSE) EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `the guidance part's allowances under §16` (`guide's allowances for the guidance part` 1500 1800 0 FALSE) EQUALS 1800
#ASSERT `the guidance part's allowances under §16` (`guide's allowances for the guidance part` 2000 1800 400 TRUE) EQUALS 2200
#ASSERT `the guidance part's allowances under §16` (`guide's allowances for the guidance part` 2500 1800 400 TRUE) EQUALS 2500

-- The clauses as they are numbered, and as §16 names them.
`the clause that pays the guidance allowance` MEANS 14
`the clause that pays the profession allowance` MEANS 15
`the clause §16(א) names for the guidance allowance` MEANS 15
`the clause §16(א) names for the profession allowance` MEANS 16
`the sub-clauses of §16` MEANS LIST "(א)", "(ב)", "(ג)", "(ד)"

`§16 names its neighbours one clause off` MEANS
        NOT (`the clause §16(א) names for the guidance allowance` EQUALS `the clause that pays the guidance allowance`)
    AND NOT (`the clause §16(א) names for the profession allowance` EQUALS `the clause that pays the profession allowance`)
    AND `the clause §16(א) names for the guidance allowance` EQUALS `the clause that pays the guidance allowance` PLUS 1
    AND NOT elem "(ה)" `the sub-clauses of §16`
#ASSERT `§16 names its neighbours one clause off`

-- (ג): the check of (א)–(ב) is made every year in September, or in the
-- guide's first month of employment in the school year, whichever is later.
@ref akn:art_16__para_c
GIVEN `the guide's first month of employment in the school year` IS A NUMBER, `the September of the school year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the month §16's check is made in` `the guide's first month of employment in the school year` `the September of the school year` IS
    max `the guide's first month of employment in the school year` `the September of the school year`

#ASSERT `the month §16's check is made in` (`guides' agreement salary month` 2016 11) (`guides' agreement salary month` 2016 9) EQUALS `guides' agreement salary month` 2016 11

-- §17: the payments of this chapter are made from the salary for February
-- 2017 (paid in March) and no later than the salary for March 2017 (paid
-- in April), with the differences from the determining date.
@ref akn:art_17/p1
`paying chapter ה` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `pay the payments of chapter ה`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the State` BECAUSE "§17: from the salary for February 2017, the March salary at the latest"

GIVEN `first paid with the salary for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `chapter ה is paid in time` `first paid with the salary for` IF
    `first paid with the salary for` AT MOST `guides' agreement salary month` 2017 3

#ASSERT `chapter ה is paid in time` (`guides' agreement salary month` 2017 3)
#ASSERT NOT `chapter ה is paid in time` (`guides' agreement salary month` 2017 4)

-- §18: for a regular guide on a budgetary pension, the guidance part's
-- determining salary follows the agreements that would apply to a teacher
-- on the terms his base salary follows; computed by weighting two periods,
-- as the letters of 11.5.2016 and 21.12.2015 say (not in the corpus: an
-- input).
@ref akn:art_18/p1 akn:art_18/p2
ASSUME `the determining salary weighted over two periods by the letters of 11.5.2016 and 21.12.2015` IS A FUNCTION FROM `terms a guide's base salary follows` TO NUMBER

GIVEN t IS A `terms a guide's base salary follows`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a regular guide's determining salary for the guidance part` t IS
    `the determining salary weighted over two periods by the letters of 11.5.2016 and 21.12.2015` t

-- §19: the agreement sets the guides' pay anew; the terms of earlier
-- agreements stand for its period unless amended or cancelled by it,
-- expressly or impliedly; the parties act in that spirit on what it did not
-- discuss.
@ref akn:art_19/p1
GIVEN `amended or cancelled by this agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an earlier term stands under the guides' agreement` `amended or cancelled by this agreement` IF
    NOT `amended or cancelled by this agreement`

@ref akn:art_19/p1
`acting in the spirit of §19` MEANS
    (PARTY `the State`
     MUST  `act in the spirit of §19 on a matter the agreement did not discuss`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     MUST  `act in the spirit of §19 on a matter the agreement did not discuss`)

-- §20(א): the agreement fully exhausts the parties' claims on what it
-- settles, the Ofek Hadash reform for the guides among them; and it
-- exhausts (1) §155(ב) of the base agreement for guides (imported), (2)
-- §90 of the completion agreement for guides (imported: §§88–89 on the
-- populations of §155(ב)), (3) §§12 and 17(ב) of the agreement of 17.9.2013
-- (not encoded here), (4) §11(ב)(1) of the agreement of 30.9.2016
-- (imported). (ב)–(ג): no further negotiation under them, nor on further
-- economic demands on the reform for the guides. (ה): no other exhaustion
-- or industrial peace is touched.
DECLARE `negotiation §20(א) exhausts` IS ONE OF
    `§155(ב) of the base agreement, for the guides`
    `§90 of the completion agreement, for the guides`
    `§§12 and 17(ב) of the agreement of 17.9.2013`
    `§11(ב)(1) of the agreement of 30.9.2016`

@ref akn:art_20 akn:art_20__para_a akn:art_20__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_20__para_a__subpara_2 akn:art_20__para_a__subpara_3 akn:art_20__para_a__subpara_4 akn:art_20__para_b akn:art_20__para_c akn:art_20__para_e
GIVEN n IS A `negotiation §20(א) exhausts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `still open after the guides' agreement` n IF
    FALSE

-- What each of the four was, in the instruments imported.
#ASSERT `may be negotiated` `the reform for further populations`
#ASSERT `§11 of the September 2016 agreement leaves open` `the reform for teaching employees in guidance roles`
#ASSERT `§§88 and 89 apply to the population` `teaching employees in guidance roles` TRUE

GIVEN p IS A `population §155(ב) leaves to negotiation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the completion agreement's §90 still opens §§88–89 after the guides' agreement for` p IF
    NOT p EQUALS `teaching employees in guidance roles`

#ASSERT NOT `the completion agreement's §90 still opens §§88–89 after the guides' agreement for` `teaching employees in guidance roles`

@ref akn:art_20__para_b akn:art_20__para_c
`no further negotiation on the guides` MEANS
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     SHANT `negotiate a matter §20(א) exhausts`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     SHANT `negotiate further economic demands on the reform for the guides`)

-- (ד): industrial peace — neither party, its members or units strikes,
-- locks out or disrupts work over what the agreement settles.
@ref akn:art_20__para_d
`industrial peace under the guides' agreement` MEANS
    (PARTY `the State`
     SHANT `strike, lock out or disrupt work over a matter the guides' agreement settles`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     SHANT `strike, lock out or disrupt work over a matter the guides' agreement settles`)

-- §21: the follow-up committee of the wages commissioner, the
-- director-general and the union's secretary-general decides disputes on
-- the agreement, finally and bindingly.
@ref akn:art_21/p1
`the guides' agreement's follow-up committee` MEANS LIST `the wages commissioner`, `the director-general`, `the union's secretary-general`

GIVEN `the committee's decision` IS A STRING, `a party's reading` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `what binds the parties of the guides' agreement` `the committee's decision` `a party's reading` IS
    `the committee's decision`

